System File Execution Location Anomaly

This threat hunting scenario focuses on identifying Windows system binaries and commonly abused LOLBins executing from unexpected or non-standard directories. Legitimate system utilities are normally executed from trusted locations such as C:\Windows\System32 or C:\Windows\SysWOW64; execution from user-writable or unusual paths may indicate a renamed or relocated binary, masquerading, process spoofing, or DLL side-loading activity.

The hunt correlates the process image name, execution path, parent process, command line, file signature, and creation location to distinguish legitimate software behavior from suspicious copies of trusted Windows binaries. Particular attention should be given to binaries launched from locations such as %TEMP%, %APPDATA%, %PUBLIC%, Downloads, or other non-system directories, especially when combined with unusual parent processes or network activity.

T1036 – Masquerading
T1574.002 – Hijack Execution Flow: DLL Side-Loading
T1218 – System Binary Proxy Execution

Cortex:
dataset = xdr_data
| filter agent_os_type = ENUM.AGENT_OS_WINDOWS
    and event_type = ENUM.PROCESS
    and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| alter proc_path = lowercase(action_process_image_path),
        proc_name = lowercase(action_process_image_name)
| filter proc_name in ("atbroker.exe", "audiodg.exe", "bcdedit.exe", "bitsadmin.exe", "certreq.exe", "certutil.exe", "cmstp.exe", "conhost.exe", "consent.exe", "cscript.exe", "csrss.exe", "dashost.exe", "defrag.exe", "dfrgui.exe", "dism.exe", "dllhost.exe", "dllhst3g.exe", "dwm.exe", "eventvwr.exe", "finger.exe", "fsquirt.exe", "logonui.exe", "lsaiso.exe", "lsass.exe", "lsm.exe", "msiexec.exe", "ntoskrnl.exe", "powershell.exe", "powershell_ise.exe", "pwsh.exe", "regsvr32.exe", "rundll32.exe", "runonce.exe", "runtimebroker.exe", "schtasks.exe", "services.exe", "sihost.exe", "smartscreen.exe", "smss.exe", "spoolsv.exe", "svchost.exe", "taskhost.exe", "taskhostw.exe", "taskmgr.exe", "userinit.exe", "werfault.exe", "werfaultsecure.exe", "wininit.exe", "winlogon.exe", "winver.exe", "wlanext.exe", "wscript.exe", "wsl.exe", "wsmprovhost.exe")
| filter proc_path not in ("c:\$windows.~bt\*", "c:\$winreagent\*", "c:\windows\softwaredistribution\*", "c:\windows\system32\*", "c:\windows\systemtemp\*", "c:\windows\syswow64\*", "c:\windows\uus\*", "c:\windows\winsxs\*")
    and proc_path not contains "\systemroot\system32\"
| filter not (proc_name = "pwsh.exe" and proc_path in ("c:\program files\powershell\7\*", "c:\program files\powershell\7-preview\*", "c:\program files\windowsapps\microsoft.powershell_*", "c:\program files\windowsapps\microsoft.powershellpreview*", "*\appdata\local\microsoft\windowsapps\microsoft.powershell*"))
| filter not (proc_name = "wsl.exe" and proc_path in ("c:\program files\windowsapps\microsoftcorporationii.windowssubsystemforlinux*", "c:\program files\wsl\*", "c:\users\*\appdata\local\microsoft\windowsapps\*"))
| fields _time, agent_hostname, actor_effective_username, action_process_image_path, action_process_image_command_line, actor_process_image_path, causality_actor_process_image_path
